*.rdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
datasets/*.rdf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Rust sources are LF. `cargo fmt` rewrites whatever it touches to LF regardless of
# what the file had, so without this the endings drift back into the diff every time
# the formatter runs — which it now does as a blocking CI check. Verified by
# restoring one CRLF file and running `cargo fmt -p datalog` over it.
#
# Scoped to `*.rs` deliberately. Six .py, six .md, LICENSE and .dockerignore are
# still CRLF; nothing formats or complains about those, so normalising them would be
# churn without a reason.
*.rs text eol=lf
